<clickhouse>
  <!--
    Lets chuser manage SQL users and grants, which is how the column grants in
    airflow/dags/access_policy.py reach the mirror (#231 phase 4).

    An XML-defined user cannot be given column-level grants: the XML format
    covers databases, dictionaries and row policies, not columns. So without
    SQL access control there is no way to withhold `email` from the dashboard
    on this store at all.

    This is a mounted file rather than the image's CLICKHOUSE_ACCESS_MANAGEMENT
    environment variable, because that variable is only read when the server
    initialises a fresh data directory. On a volume that already exists it is
    silently ignored, which is a setting that appears to be applied and is not.

    The filename has to sort after default-user.xml. Files in users.d are
    merged in alphabetical order and the image writes access_management=0
    there, so an 01 prefix loses and a zz prefix wins.

    chuser is hardcoded because it is fixed in both k8s/generate-secrets.sh
    and k8s/01-secrets.yaml, where only the password is generated. A guard in
    scripts/ci/test_access_policy.py fails the build if that stops being true.
  -->
  <users>
    <chuser>
      <access_management>1</access_management>
    </chuser>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
